Assuming you're using Nethack 3.1.3 for DOS, you CAN set your own
colours in the nethack.cnf file. Add this line:

   VIDEOCOLORS = 4 2 6 1 5 3 15 12 10 14 9 13 11

The above option is the default colour scheme. It tells the hardware
which shades to use when it displays these colours (in order): red,
green, brown, blue, magenta, cyan, bright white, bright red, bright
green, yellow, bright blue, bright magenta, bright cyan. To change the
shade used to display blue -- the fourth parameter -- you would
substitute one of the other colours. For example, to have blue display
as bright cyan, change the 1 above to 11. These changes are global, so
floating eyes, fountains, water nymphs, etc. would all appear as bright
cyan.

Was that suitably confusing <grin>?

